Z||000000||chris6878||02-29-2000||05:07 PM||||I have been noticing this 88 Gt everyday when i go to college... It looked to be in mint condition (even though i like the notchbacks). A few days ago i noticed the it had been wrecked.. the drivers side is messed up pretty bad... I was curious and i stopped to look at it today... (to see what he wanted for the black factory rims on it). It looks like it may be repairable...  but the guy said he would have to wait about a week to see if the insurance company totals it.. which i think is what will happen...    what would be a good price for these rims..  they are the black honeycomb type, 15' with decent tires... ?     he may even give me a deal on the car if it is considered totaled...  it looks mint, until you walk around to the other side of it..   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">||||reg||9
Z||000001||theogre||02-29-2000||07:20 PM||||Here's how totalled works.<P>If it's totaled it belongs to the insurance company. He cannot legally remove or sell the wheels, or anything else, unless he first buys the car back from them.<P>It will then have a salvage tittle. You can repair a car with a salvage tittle but putting it back on the road can be a real big pain. How big a pain depends on your states laws.<P>Unless he wants to get rid of it he should look at the insurance offer very carefully. A non total offer may pay less but keeps the tittle clean. Also, accepting a total could drive up his own rate even if this was caused by someone else. He should consult his own insurance before accepting any offer from someone who hit him.<P>If the offers for total and not total are close offer him the dif between the 2 and take the whole car.<P>If it's just body damage most of that is not hard to fix. just time consuming. get a picture of it if you can and post it. If nothing else you can strip the whole car for parts and shove allot of it in the attic.<p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 02-29-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||chris6878||02-29-2000||08:51 PM||||If only i had a digital camera...   i am going to check back with him in a week or so...    i dont preferably like the fastbacks... but the 88gt was the last one made...  makes them a little unique....    this is actually the first time i have ever seen a fastback up close....   all mine are notch's  (84 coupe, 85 SE with gt skirts and front and rear fascia's, and an 85 GT...   so some of the mody may work... engine would....  i will check him out.. may get a good deal.....   i let u guys no how it comes...     <P>chris........||||reg||3
Z||000003||bHooper||02-29-2000||09:59 PM||||Chris, which tranny does the car have?  If it has the 5 speed and it is in decent shape, I would consider buying that from you/him/whoever winds up witht he car!  <P>Tell us scavengers more  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P><BR>Brian ||||reg||1
