Z||000008||JetroGT||03-02-2000||05:12 AM||||Too bad you don't live in Wisconsin. The state already sent me a new title for my 87 GT. The insurance company totaled it and sold it to the car dealer. The dealer then sold it to me along with a junk title. About 3 weeks later I got a letter from the DMV stating that because the car was over 7 years old and was damaged over 70% of it's market value that I did not have to get it inspected and that they would be sending me a new title in the mail, which I now have. Good luck.||||reg||1
Z||000009||Phil||03-02-2000||07:35 AM||||Even better in Rhode Island. No title is required if the car is over 10 yrs old all you need is a bill of sale.||||reg||1
